{"evidence":[{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Ghalti (Tv serial) is a Pakistani television romantic and social Islamic issue drama serial that aired on A-Plus TV from July 14, 2016 to October 7, 2016.","title":"Ghalti"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" It was directed by Kaleem Rajput and written by Iftikhar Ahmed Usmani.","title":"Ghalti"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" It is a story of two sisters who do not live together and are even unaware of the fact that they are sisters.","title":"Ghalti"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" One of them lives with their parents and the other has been adopted by her aunt.","title":"Ghalti"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" As they grow up, their cousin enters the scene.","title":"Ghalti"},{"sentence_id":5,"text":" While the family wants to marry him with the one who lives her parents, he loves the other sister.","title":"Ghalti"},{"sentence_id":6,"text":" He marries them both without telling anyone unaware that they are real sisters.","title":"Ghalti"},{"sentence_id":7,"text":" Many people are still not aware of limitations in our religion that two sisters can be married the same man at the same time.","title":"Ghalti"},{"sentence_id":8,"text":" How certain mistakes in life can outturn the whole scenario.","title":"Ghalti"},{"sentence_id":9,"text":" Ghalti has an ensemble cast with Agha Ali as Saim, Sania Shamshad as Zara Sidra Batool as Saman in leading roles, with the supporting cast Abid Ali as Ikhlaque Ahmed, Sajida Syed, Shehryar Zaidi, Lubna Aslam, and Naila Jaffery, The show is set in Karachi, Sindh.","title":"Ghalti"},{"sentence_id":10,"text":" It remained popular throughout its run.","title":"Ghalti"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Gauhar Ali (born 5 May 1989) is a Pakistani first-class cricketer who plays for Peshawar.","title":"Gauhar Ali"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" He made 145 not out in the final of the 2016–17 Regional One Day Cup and was jointly named man of the match along with Iftikhar Ahmed.","title":"Gauhar Ali"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Shafilea Iftikhar Ahmed (14 July 1986 – 11 September 2003) was a 17-year-old British Pakistani girl from Great Sankey, Warrington, Cheshire, who was murdered by her parents Iftikhar and Farzana Ahmed.","title":"Murder of Shafilea Ahmed"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" They were imprisoned for a minimum of 25 years each in 2012.","title":"Murder of Shafilea Ahmed"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" The possibility of others having helped them to dispose of her body was raised; after the trial, the Chief Executive of the Bradford Council for Mosques encouraged anybody with information about the case to come forward, and said his group would help police.","title":"Murder of Shafilea Ahmed"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Zahid Iftikhar Ahmed (born September 20, 1984) is a Pakistani television actor and former RJ.","title":"Zahid Ahmed (actor)"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" Ahmed worked as a creative manager for PTV World, and later became an RJ.","title":"Zahid Ahmed (actor)"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" Although successful, he left it to pursue a career in acting, and made his broadway debut with a leading role in the play "It Runs in the Family" (2006).","title":"Zahid Ahmed (actor)"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" He received widespread acclaim for his portrayal of Muhammad Ali Jinnah in Anwar Maqsood's, "Sawa 14 August" and its sequel "Pawnay 14 August" (both 2014).","title":"Zahid Ahmed (actor)"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" That same year, he made his television debut with the Hum TV romantic series "Mehram".","title":"Zahid Ahmed (actor)"},{"sentence_id":5,"text":" His breakout role in the Hum TV series "Alvida" (2015), garnered him the Hum Award for Best Villain, and a nomination for Best Supporting Actor.","title":"Zahid Ahmed (actor)"},{"sentence_id":6,"text":" Subsequently, he received wide recognition for his portrayal of leading roles in several of the successful series, including "Jugnoo" (2015), "Tum Mere Paas Raho" (2015), "Sangat" (2015), "Zara Yaad Kar" (2016) and "Besharam" (2016).","title":"Zahid Ahmed (actor)"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Iftikhar Ahmed (Bengali: ইফতেখার আহমেদ ) a development economist and author, is the first Bangladeshi born Swiss lawmaker.","title":"Iftikhar Ahmed (Swiss lawmaker)"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" He is a former International Labour Organization (ILO) official.","title":"Iftikhar Ahmed (Swiss lawmaker)"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Admiral Iftikhar Ahmed Sirohey (Urdu: ایڈمرل افتخار احمد سروہی; b. 1934) , is a retired four-star rank admiral, strategist, and a memoirist who is currently tenuring his fellowship at the Institute of Strategic Studies (ISS) in Islamabad, Pakistan.","title":"Iftikhar Ahmed Sirohey"}],"peer_messages":["Unverified peer answer: Pakistan and Switzerland
