{"evidence":[{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Deckenia is a genus of freshwater crabs from East Africa, in the family Potamonautidae, or sometimes in a family of its own, Deckeniidae.","title":"Deckenia (crab)"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" The genus was named by Hilgendorf after Karl Klaus von der Decken who collected the first examples during his expeditions to Africa.","title":"Deckenia (crab)"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" Both species live in swamps from Eyl in Somalia to Dar es Salaam, Tanzania, both in coastal areas and further inland.","title":"Deckenia (crab)"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" A third species, "Deckenia alluaudi", lives in the Seychelles, and has been transferred to a separate genus, "Seychellum".","title":"Deckenia (crab)"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Miltoniopsis vexillaria ("the flag-like "Miltoniopsis"") is a species of epiphytic orchid in the genus Miltoniopsis.","title":"Miltoniopsis vexillaria"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Miltoniopsis, abbreviated Mltnps in horticultural trade, is a genus of orchids native to Costa Rica, Panama, Venezuela, Colombia, Ecuador, and Peru.","title":"Miltoniopsis"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" This genus comprises 5 species.","title":"Miltoniopsis"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" Miltoniopsis's common name is Pansy Orchid.","title":"Miltoniopsis"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Strobilanthes is a genus of about 350 species of flowering plants in the family Acanthaceae, mostly native to tropical Asia and Madagascar, but with a few species extending north into temperate regions of Asia.","title":"Strobilanthes"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" Many species are cultivated for their 2-lipped, hooded flowers in shades of blue, pink, white and purple.","title":"Strobilanthes"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" Most are frost-tender and require protection in frost-prone areas.","title":"Strobilanthes"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Strobilanthes japonica is a flowering herbaceous perennial plant from Asia, one of around 350 plants of the genus "Strobilanthes".","title":"Strobilanthes japonica"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" The 20–50 cm ornamental plant is cultivated in Japan and China, and blooms in autumn with 1.5 cm purple to white funnel-shaped flowers.","title":"Strobilanthes japonica"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Nematops is a genus of righteye flounders native to the Indo-West Pacific.","title":"Nematops"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" Due to their small size (up to 10 cm ) and depth of habitation (up to 650 m ) few examples of this genus are caught, and as a result little is known of their morphology and distribution.","title":"Nematops"}],"peer_messages":["Unverified peer answer: Yes
